---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Shanghai's Top Hospitals for Pancreatic Cancer Surgery | MedInSh"
			description="Detailed profiles of Shanghai's leading hepatobiliary-pancreatic surgical centers. Fudan Cancer Center, Ruijin Hospital, Huashan Hospital, Changhai Hospital and Shanghai First People's Hospital."
		/>
		<style>
			.page-header {
				text-align: center;
				padding: 3em 0 2em;
				border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
				margin-bottom: 2.5em;
			}
			.page-header h1 { font-size: 2.2em; margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
			.page-header p { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0; }

			/* Hospital section */
			.hospital-section {
				margin-bottom: 4em;
				padding-bottom: 4em;
				border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
			}
			.hospital-section:last-child {
				border-bottom: none;
				margin-bottom: 0;
				padding-bottom: 0;
			}
			.hospital-header {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 320px 1fr;
				gap: 2em;
				margin-bottom: 1.5em;
			}
			.hospital-img {
				border-radius: 10px;
				overflow: hidden;
				box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
			}
			.hospital-img img {
				width: 100%;
				height: 220px;
				object-fit: cover;
				display: block;
				border-radius: 0;
			}
			.hospital-basic h2 {
				font-size: 1.8em;
				margin: 0 0 0.15em;
			}
			.hospital-cn {
				font-size: 1.1em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
				margin: 0 0 0.4em;
			}
			.hospital-badge {
				display: inline-block;
				padding: 0.15em 0.6em;
				background: var(--accent-light);
				color: var(--accent);
				border-radius: 3px;
				font-size: 0.75em;
				font-weight: 700;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				margin-bottom: 0.5em;
			}
			.hospital-affil {
				font-size: 0.9em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
				margin: 0;
			}

			/* Stats row */
			.stats-row {
				display: flex;
				gap: 0.8em;
				margin: 1em 0 1.5em;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
			}
			.stat-pill {
				background: white;
				border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
				border-radius: 8px;
				padding: 0.7em 1em;
				text-align: center;
				min-width: 100px;
				flex: 1;
			}
			.stat-pill .val {
				display: block;
				font-size: 1.3em;
				font-weight: 700;
				color: var(--accent);
				line-height: 1.1;
			}
			.stat-pill .lbl {
				font-size: 0.7em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray));
				margin-top: 0.15em;
			}

			/* Detail text */
			.hospital-detail {
				font-size: 0.95em;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
				line-height: 1.7;
				max-width: 780px;
			}
			.hospital-detail h3 {
				font-size: 1.15em;
				margin: 1.5em 0 0.5em;
				color: var(--accent-dark);
			}
			.hospital-detail ul {
				padding-left: 1.2em;
			}
			.hospital-detail li {
				margin-bottom: 0.4em;
			}

			/* International highlight box */
			.highlight-box {
				background: var(--green-light);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--green);
				padding: 1em 1.5em;
				border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
				margin: 1.5em 0;
				font-size: 0.95em;
			}
			.highlight-box strong { color: var(--accent-dark); }

			/* CTA */
			.hospital-cta {
				display: inline-block;
				margin-top: 1em;
				padding: 0.6em 1.4em;
				background: var(--accent);
				color: white;
				text-decoration: none;
				border-radius: 6px;
				font-weight: 700;
				font-size: 0.9em;
				transition: background 0.2s;
			}
			.hospital-cta:hover { background: var(--accent-dark); color: white; }

			@media (max-width: 720px) {
				.hospital-header { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
				.hospital-img { max-height: 200px; }
				.stats-row { flex-wrap: wrap; }
				.stat-pill { min-width: calc(50% - 0.4em); }
				.hospital-basic h2 { font-size: 1.4em; }
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="page-header">
				<h1>Hospitals</h1>
				<p>Shanghai's leading centers for hepatobiliary-pancreatic surgery — detailed profiles, surgical volumes, and international patient services.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- ===== Fudan Cancer Center ===== -->
			<div class="hospital-section">
				<div class="hospital-header">
					<div class="hospital-img">
						<img src="/images/fudan-hospital.jpg" alt="Fudan University Shanghai Cancer Center" />
					</div>
					<div class="hospital-basic">
						<span class="hospital-badge">Comprehensive Oncology</span>
						<h2>Fudan University Shanghai Cancer Center</h2>
						<p class="hospital-cn">复旦大学附属肿瘤医院</p>
						<p class="hospital-affil">Affiliated with Fudan University · Founded 1931 · Grade III, Class A Oncology Hospital</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="stats-row">
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">3,000+</span><span class="lbl">Complex surgeries/year</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">80,000</span><span class="lbl">Surgeries/year (total)</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">72%</span><span class="lbl">5-year survival rate</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">250万</span><span class="lbl">Outpatient visits/year</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">2,177</span><span class="lbl">Hospital beds</span></div>
				</div>

				<div class="hospital-detail">
					<p>
						Fudan University Shanghai Cancer Center (FUSCC) is China's earliest established oncology hospital and Shanghai's only tertiary Grade A hospital dedicated exclusively to cancer. The pancreatic surgery department, led by <strong>Prof. Yu Xianjun (虞先濬)</strong> and <strong>Dr. Xu Xiaowu (徐晓武)</strong>, is a national leader in minimally invasive pancreatic surgery.
					</p>

					<h3>Pancreatic Surgery Highlights</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Over 1,000 Whipple procedures per year — among the highest volumes globally</li>
						<li>80%+ minimally invasive rate (laparoscopic and robotic)</li>
						<li>20%+ of cases involve vascular resection & reconstruction — demonstrating mastery of complex cases</li>
						<li>Live-streamed laparoscopic Whipple demonstrations at the 36th Italian Digestive Surgery Congress (Milan, 2025), earning international praise as "textbook-level"</li>
						<li>Innovated "middle approach laparoscopic Whipple" (Leave the Vein Alone concept) — reducing blood loss and complications</li>
						<li>Pancreatic duct-mucosa double-layer anastomosis technique for safer reconstruction</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Equipment & Technology</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Da Vinci surgical robot system</li>
						<li>Proton and heavy ion therapy (integrated with Shanghai Proton and Heavy Ion Center)</li>
						<li>PET-CT, PET-MR, 5.0T MRI — 22 high-end imaging devices</li>
						<li>National drug clinical trial institution — hundreds of active oncology trials</li>
						<li>AI-powered precision oncology platform</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Clinical Trials & Innovation</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>695 new clinical trials in 2025 alone (75% investigator-initiated)</li>
						<li>National Natural Science Foundation: 100 projects funded in 2025</li>
						<li>Published 35 papers with IF ≥ 20 in top journals including BMJ and Nature</li>
						<li>Clinical research funding: ~600M RMB/year</li>
						<li>17 international guideline changes per year — shaping global oncology standards</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>International Recognition</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Cooperation agreements with 10+ institutions in France, Italy, Japan, Russia, Singapore</li>
						<li>Top A rating in national hospital performance for oncology — consistently</li>
						<li>Sister department relationship with UM/Sylvester Comprehensive Cancer Center (Miami)</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="highlight-box">
						<strong>Why international patients choose FUSCC:</strong> The sheer surgical volume (3,000+ complex cases/year) means the team encounters rare and difficult presentations weekly that other centers see yearly. This depth of experience is the single strongest predictor of surgical outcomes.
					</div>

					<a href="/medical-travel" class="hospital-cta">Plan Your Visit to FUSCC →</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ===== Ruijin Hospital ===== -->
			<div class="hospital-section">
				<div class="hospital-header">
					<div class="hospital-img">
						<img src="/images/ruijin-team.jpg" alt="Ruijin Hospital pancreatic disease center" />
					</div>
					<div class="hospital-basic">
						<span class="hospital-badge">Pancreatic Disease Center</span>
						<h2>Ruijin Hospital</h2>
						<p class="hospital-cn">上海交通大学医学院附属瑞金医院</p>
						<p class="hospital-affil">Affiliated with Shanghai Jiao Tong University · Founded 1907 · Grade III, Class A</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="stats-row">
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">30,000+</span><span class="lbl">Pancreatic cancer cases (cumulative)</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">2,000+</span><span class="lbl">Complex surgeries/year</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">21.2%</span><span class="lbl">5-year survival (vs 9-12% global)</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">35.3%</span><span class="lbl">5-year survival (Stage I)</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">3,000+</span><span class="lbl">Da Vinci robotic surgeries</span></div>
				</div>

				<div class="hospital-detail">
					<p>
						Ruijin Hospital is home to the world's largest, fully integrated, one-stop pancreatic disease diagnosis and treatment center. Led by <strong>Prof. Shen Baiyong (沈柏用)</strong>, Vice President of Ruijin Hospital and Director of the Pancreatic Disease Center, the center has treated over 30,000 pancreatic cancer cases — the largest quantity in the world.
					</p>

					<h3>Key Achievements</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>5-year survival rate of 21.2% — nearly double the global average of 9–12%</li>
						<li>Stage I 5-year survival: 35.3% — a new global benchmark</li>
						<li>Over 3,000 Da Vinci robotic pancreatic surgeries completed (malignant tumors: 2,000+)</li>
						<li>Prof. Shen: first and only Chinese expert to co-author the ESMO Asia-Pacific Pancreatic Cancer Consensus</li>
						<li>12 high-risk biomarkers monitored — 3–6 month early warning window for tumor detection</li>
						<li>Personalized pancreatic cancer vaccine in Phase III clinical trials</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>International Partnership</h3>
					<p>
						In 2025, Ruijin established the <strong>Ruijin · United Family International Pancreatic Center</strong>
						in partnership with United Family Healthcare — an international medical platform explicitly designed
						to serve global patients. The partnership connects Ruijin's clinical excellence with international
						healthcare networks across the UK, UAE, and beyond.
					</p>

					<h3>MDT Model</h3>
					<p>
						The center integrates pancreatic surgery, medical oncology, ICU, interventional radiology,
						endoscopy, pathology, and precision medicine into a single multidisciplinary team — the same
						model used by top Western cancer centers.
					</p>

					<div class="highlight-box">
						<strong>Prof. Shen Baiyong:</strong> "Having treated over 30,000 pancreatic cancer cases, the largest quantity in the world, our center has become a global leader in comprehensive care on the disease. The five-year survival rate at our center is 21.2 percent, almost doubling the global average." — <em>Shanghai Daily / City News Service, May 2025</em>
					</div>

					<a href="/doctors" class="hospital-cta">Meet Ruijin's Surgeons →</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ===== Huashan Hospital ===== -->
			<div class="hospital-section">
				<div class="hospital-header">
					<div class="hospital-img">
						<img src="/images/shanghai-hospital.jpg" alt="Huashan Hospital" />
					</div>
					<div class="hospital-basic">
						<span class="hospital-badge">General Surgery / Pancreatic</span>
						<h2>Huashan Hospital</h2>
						<p class="hospital-cn">复旦大学附属华山医院</p>
						<p class="hospital-affil">Affiliated with Fudan University · Founded 1907 · Grade III, Class A</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="stats-row">
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">1907</span><span class="lbl">Established</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">Fudan</span><span class="lbl">University Affiliated</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">Intl Ward</span><span class="lbl">English-speaking staff</span></div>
				</div>

				<div class="hospital-detail">
					<p>
						Huashan Hospital is one of Fudan University's flagship teaching hospitals with strong general surgery and growing pancreatic expertise. The hospital's international department provides dedicated services for overseas patients.
					</p>

					<h3>Why Consider Huashan</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Strong general surgery department with hepatobiliary-pancreatic capabilities</li>
						<li>International patient ward with English-speaking coordinators</li>
						<li>Part of the Fudan University hospital system — cross-referral with Fudan Cancer Center available</li>
						<li>Well-established infrastructure for international patients</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ===== Changhai Hospital ===== -->
			<div class="hospital-section">
				<div class="hospital-header">
					<div class="hospital-img">
						<img src="/images/hospital-interior.jpg" alt="Changhai Hospital" />
					</div>
					<div class="hospital-basic">
						<span class="hospital-badge">Hepatobiliary / Pancreatic</span>
						<h2>Changhai Hospital</h2>
						<p class="hospital-cn">海军军医大学附属长海医院</p>
						<p class="hospital-affil">Affiliated with Naval Medical University · Grade III, Class A</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="stats-row">
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">Military</span><span class="lbl">Medical University</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">High</span><span class="lbl">Surgical Volume</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">Civilian</span><span class="lbl">Access Available</span></div>
				</div>

				<div class="hospital-detail">
					<p>
						Changhai Hospital, affiliated with the Naval Medical University (formerly Second Military Medical University), has a strong hepatobiliary-pancreatic surgery department with high surgical volumes.
					</p>

					<h3>Why Consider Changhai</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>High-volume hepatobiliary and pancreatic surgery</li>
						<li>Military-affiliated hospital with strict quality standards</li>
						<li>International patients can access services with appropriate coordination</li>
						<li>Strong academic research program in hepato-pancreato-biliary surgery</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ===== Nanjing Drum Tower Hospital ===== -->
			<div class="hospital-section">
				<div class="hospital-header">
					<div class="hospital-img">
						<img src="/images/drum-tower-3d-print.jpg" alt="Nanjing Drum Tower Hospital 3D-printed pancreatic cancer model" />
					</div>
					<div class="hospital-basic">
						<span class="hospital-badge">Pancreatic-Biliary Oncology</span>
						<h2>Nanjing Drum Tower Hospital</h2>
						<p class="hospital-cn">南京大学医学院附属鼓楼医院</p>
						<p class="hospital-affil">Affiliated with Nanjing University Medicine School · Founded 1892 · Three campuses · 4,600+ beds</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="stats-row">
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">1892</span><span class="lbl">Established</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">4,600+</span><span class="lbl">Beds across 3 campuses</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">High-level</span><span class="lbl">Jiangsu hospital construction unit</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">PAAG</span><span class="lbl">ASCO GI 2026 regimen</span></div>
				</div>

				<div class="hospital-detail">
					<p>
						Nanjing Drum Tower Hospital is the Affiliated Hospital of Nanjing University Medicine School. Founded in 1892, it is one of the earliest Western hospitals in China and has grown into a large-scale comprehensive tertiary hospital with a full range of disciplines, advanced medical technology, and strong research capability.
					</p>

					<h3>Historical Background</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Established in 1892, making it one of the earliest Western hospitals in China</li>
						<li>Now operates three campuses: Main Campus in Drum Tower District, Jiangbei, and Southern branch</li>
						<li>Serves as a pilot hospital for high-quality development of public hospitals in China</li>
						<li>Recognized as a high-level hospital construction unit in Jiangsu Province</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Technical Strengths</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Full-discipline comprehensive tertiary hospital with advanced medical technology infrastructure</li>
						<li>Strong research platform spanning clinical research, education, and translational medicine</li>
						<li>Uses advanced imaging, multidisciplinary review, and 3D planning for complex pancreatic-biliary cases</li>
						<li>International collaboration and training capacity, including overseas specialist visits and joint programs</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Oncology Center Expertise</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>The Cancer Center includes a dedicated pancreatic-biliary oncology subspecialty</li>
						<li>Led by <strong>Prof. Du Juan (杜娟)</strong>, the team focuses on metastatic pancreatic cancer and integrated systemic therapy</li>
						<li>PAAG regimen research was selected for the 2026 ASCO Gastrointestinal Cancers Symposium</li>
						<li>Clinical output includes randomized trial data, precision oncology strategies, and publication in top international journals</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="highlight-box">
						<strong>Why international patients should know this center:</strong> Drum Tower combines a 130-year institutional history with modern oncology infrastructure, making it one of the most established and academically active pancreatic cancer centers in eastern China.
					</div>

					<a href="/oncologists" class="hospital-cta">Meet Prof. Du Juan →</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- ===== Shanghai First People's Hospital ===== -->
			<div class="hospital-section">
				<div class="hospital-header">
					<div class="hospital-img">
						<img src="/images/medical-tech.jpg" alt="Shanghai First People's Hospital" />
					</div>
					<div class="hospital-basic">
						<span class="hospital-badge">Pancreatic Center</span>
						<h2>Shanghai First People's Hospital</h2>
						<p class="hospital-cn">上海市第一人民医院胰腺中心</p>
						<p class="hospital-affil">Affiliated with Shanghai Jiao Tong University · Grade III, Class A</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="stats-row">
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">SJU</span><span class="lbl">Affiliated</span></div>
					<div class="stat-pill"><span class="val">Pancreatic</span><span class="lbl">Dedicated Center</span></div>
				</div>

				<div class="hospital-detail">
					<p>
						Shanghai First People's Hospital (Shanghai General Hospital) operates a dedicated pancreatic center as part of its surgical oncology program. The hospital is affiliated with Shanghai Jiao Tong University.
					</p>

					<h3>Why Consider Shanghai First People's</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Dedicated pancreatic center — not just a department within general surgery</li>
						<li>University-affiliated with strong research capabilities</li>
						<li>Growing international patient services</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>

		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
